# Language

- All responses, code, comments, commit-related content, and documentation MUST be written in English.
- Do NOT use any other language unless explicitly requested.

# General Behaviour

- Be concise, practical, and precise.
- Prefer clarity and maintainability over cleverness.
- Do not invent project-specific requirements, behaviour, architecture, or business rules.
- When a project-specific requirement is unclear and cannot be determined from the documentation or established codebase patterns, treat it as TBD and ask for clarification.
- For ordinary implementation details, use established codebase patterns and standard engineering practices instead of asking unnecessary questions.
- Do not leave TODOs, placeholders, incomplete implementations, or commented-out temporary code unless explicitly requested.
- Do not make changes outside the scope of the current task.